 ```
 
+When a parameter you need isn't available in [`ModelSettings`][agents.models.interface.ModelSettings], you can use `extra_args` to pass arbitrary keyword arguments straight through to the underlying model provider's API. For example, when you use OpenAI's Responses API, [there are a few other optional parameters](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/responses/create) (e.g., `user`, `service_tier`, and so on) that you can pass this way.
+
+```python
+from agents import Agent, ModelSettings
+
+english_agent = Agent(
+    name="English agent",
+    instructions="You only speak English",
+    model="gpt-4o",
+    model_settings=ModelSettings(
+        temperature=0.1,
+        extra_args={"service_tier": "flex", "user": "user_12345"},
+    ),
+)
+```
+
+`extra_args` from [`RunConfig.model_settings`][agents.run.RunConfig.model_settings] are merged with the agent's own `extra_args` rather than replacing them, with the run config winning if the same key appears in both. Any `None` values are filtered out before the request is made.
+
+!!! warning
+
+    Not all model providers support all parameters. Passing a parameter that a provider doesn't recognize may cause an error, so check the API documentation for the specific model and provider you are using.
+
 ## Common issues with using other LLM providers
 
